{"ideas":[{"id":"idea_01","risks":"This may only produce theorem hygiene rather than new insight. The bridge still depends on standard measurable-version facts and can easily overclaim behavioral equivalence instead of reward-coordinate equality.","suggested_lenses":["proof strategy","measure-theory audit"],"summary":"Complete the original Borel-policy no-gap bridge under the exact finite-grid public-exogenous seed/state model. Prove both inclusions between common Borel randomized policies and completed public-prefix kernels: forward via seed/prefix induction and Fubini; reverse via Borel versions of completed kernels, simplex repair on null sets, and finite-action randomization.","title":"Close Borel No-Gap Bridge","why_promising":"This is one of the few remaining gaps in an otherwise coherent finite/no-gap theorem package. A successful explorer could turn a conditional partial result into a referee-ready theorem with clear scope."},{"id":"idea_02","risks":"Even if fully proved, it remains an abstract value identity, not a structural tail condition. It may not advance rates unless paired with examples where the ba witness can be computed.","suggested_lenses":["proof strategy","functional-analysis audit","example computation"],"summary":"Write the finitely additive finite-grid dual as a standalone proposition and stress-test it on known infinite-class gap examples. Verify the norm-separation proof, positivity of the separator, normalization to a finitely additive probability, and the relation between finite-prior/product-closure value and true ba value.","title":"Referee-Proof ba Dual","why_promising":"The solver attempt relies on this as the exact arbitrary-class finite-grid value. A precise proof plus worked examples would clarify exactly what the abstract characterization buys and where it stops."},{"id":"idea_03","risks":"The desired comparator-specific delay bound may be false. Prior clipped-Hedge and nested-oracle routes failed, so this needs either a genuinely new potential or a crisp counterexample.","suggested_lenses":["algorithm design","counterexample search"],"summary":"Attack the two-arm delayed-advantage problem directly: find an algorithm or impossibility result for ensuring both A_T >= -tilde O(sqrt(T)) and A_T >= S_T - tilde O(sqrt(TD)). Focus on reserve/fractional-wealth rules or a direct potential that avoids capacity depletion.","title":"Delayed Advantage Safety and Capture","why_promising":"This is the minimal test for tail-adaptive truncation. Proving or refuting it would settle whether the adaptive upper bound can come from comparator-specific heterogeneous-delay experts."},{"id":"idea_04","risks":"Naive repetitions already collapse through comparator averaging, one-reveal learning, and persistent quote cross-hits. The construction may hit an information-theoretic tradeoff that prevents matching the upper rate.","suggested_lenses":["lower bound","information theory","construction audit"],"summary":"Build and evaluate limited-leakage lower-rate families for power-tail envelopes. Start with noisy common-parameter or codebook terminal signals where tail events have mass q, revenue separation gamma, and terminal information KL kappa; compute the finite-grid Bayes value before embedding into market prices.","title":"Limited-Leakage Tail Lower Bounds","why_promising":"Matching power-tail lower rates is still the main open rate question. This direction directly targets the known failure modes of repeated q-scaled terminal atoms."},{"id":"idea_05","risks":"May yield only another sufficient condition, not necessity. Hidden/labeled examples show any condition ignoring public-prefix predictability is doomed.","suggested_lenses":["proof strategy","counterexample search"],"summary":"Develop a last-exceedance/value-tail calculus using L_a = max{s <= T: P_s > a}. Express comparator value and truncation gaps through last-exceedance ages, then add a public-prefix predictability term to see whether it gives sharper sufficient bounds or cleaner lower-bound certificates.","title":"Predictable Last-Exceedance Tails","why_promising":"The identity sum_t r_t(a)=a(L_a-1)_+ is algebraically exact and may expose value-weighted tail quantities that first-hitting beta obscures."},{"id":"idea_06","risks":"Could end as another boundary counterexample rather than a positive theorem. The horizon-aware oracle already solves known finite-horizon laws, so the model must be carefully horizon-free.","suggested_lenses":["counterexample search","model taxonomy"],"summary":"Formalize the anytime known-law obstruction using super-growing deterministic two-deadline blocks. Prove or refute that no single horizon-free policy can get sublinear regret at all horizons even when the infinite exogenous sequence is known.","title":"Anytime Known-Law Boundary","why_promising":"It would sharpen the model taxonomy and explain exactly how much of the known-law oracle depends on horizon awareness."},{"id":"idea_07","risks":"Natural Borel counterexamples may not exist, or may be solved by identifiability rather than compactness. Weak/Feller continuity alone is already known insufficient for the compactness proof.","suggested_lenses":["counterexample search","proof strategy","measurability audit"],"summary":"Search for natural infinite-class no-gap hypotheses beyond payoff-measure domination. Either prove useful sufficient conditions such as identifiable Borel parameter classes or dominated approximations with explicit constants, or find a Borel nondominated non-identifiable class where finite subclasses are easy but the full class has linear value.","title":"Natural Infinite-Class No-Gap Criteria","why_promising":"The current non-Borel gap is pathological and payoff-measure domination is only sufficient. A natural theorem or natural obstruction would substantially improve the characterization."}],"solution_status":"unsolved"}
